    "body": "## Motivation\n\n`--decrypted-draft-config-file` reaches `get_config` as `_configuration_file`, and `AutoConfig.from_pretrained` applies it. For model types in `_CONFIG_REGISTRY` (DeepSeek-V4 among them), the config is then reloaded from the checkpoint without that kwarg, so the override is silently dropped. A DSpark draft whose quantization differs from the target's, for example a block-FP8 draft next to a per-channel FP8 target, then loads with the target's config.\n\n## Modifications\n\n`HfModelConfigParser.parse` passes `_configuration_file` through the registry reload (5 lines in `utils/hf_transformers/config.py`).\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nOn main `def8f93212` with this change and #47886 (which this target needs to load on gfx942), DeepSeek-V4-Flash FP8 per-channel target with its block-FP8 draft config, DSpark block size 5, TP4 on MI308X: the draft config is honored, accept length is 4.6-5.5 at 1024-token outputs, and gsm8k 8-shot on all 1319 questions scores 0.9431. Not A/B'd on main without the fix; on an older SGLang tree without it, the draft fell back to the target's config and accept length dropped to about 1.0.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot applicable: config loading only.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41415744291](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41415744291)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41415744266](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41415744266)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41415744002](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41415744002)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
